Here's the logic mapping from C to Rust:

| C behavior | Rust equivalent |
|---|---|
| dst == NULL \|\| numElem == 0 → return 22 | dst.is_null() \|\| num_elem == 0 → return 22 |
| src == NULL → dst[0] = 0, return 22 | Same, via unsafe { *dst = 0 } |
| Scan ptr forward to find null terminator in dst | Same pointer walk with ptr < dst_end && *ptr != 0 |
| Copy src into dst at ptr, return 0 on null byte | Same loop, return 0 when ch == 0 |
| Buffer overflow → dst[0] = 0, return 34 (ERANGE) | Same fallthrough after loop exhausts num_elem |

